# Case of the Filched Falcon: "When this Case enters, investigate" gives Bot1 a Clue on turn 1. "To solve - You control three or more artifacts" (CR 719.3a, an intervening
# "if", CR 603.4): at the turn-1 end step Bot1 controls two artifacts (Mox Sapphire and the Clue), so it does not solve. At Bot1's turn-3 end step it still controls two while
# Bot2 controls four (Mox Ruby, Mox Jet, Ornithopter, Memnite): the opponent's artifacts do not count. On turn 5 Bot1 casts Mox Jet: exactly three (Sapphire, Jet, the Clue,
# the Island is not an artifact) and before the end step the Case's ability is refused though {2}{U} could be paid (it is not solved); at the end step it becomes solved
# (CR 719.3a), and from then on the ability is offered.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Case of the Filched Falcon
Island
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Memnite
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Case of the Filched Falcon.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Clue Token.Token = true
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Filched Falcon.Solved = (absent)
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Filched Falcon.Solved = (absent)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
! Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Filched Falcon.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby)
[T5 Bot1.End]
? Stack.Count = 1
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Filched Falcon.Solved = true

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Case of the Filched Falcon; Clue Token; Island; Mox Jet; Mox Sapphire
